</figure>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.21790v1/Figs/chunk_lengths_error.png" id="A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:274/211;" width="274" height="211" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Prediction error distribution of the dynamic router. The router achieved a 91.4% accuracy rate, demonstrating its effectiveness in expert selection.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.21790v1/Ablation_LIBERO.png" id="A1.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/331;" width="548" height="331" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Visualization of the ablation study on LIBERO dataset. We compare LongScape with variants using only fixed-length chunks. These fixed-length approaches often exhibit discontinuous or physically implausible actions. In contrast, LongScape, by incorporating an adaptive expert mechanism, ensures action coherence and stable generation.</figcaption>
</figure>
